1
00:00:00,659 --> 00:00:02,159
(Leonard(on phone):)Got it.

2
00:00:02,761 --> 00:00:04,331
(Vet:)Should have been a dentist.

3
00:00:06,298 --> 00:00:10,208
OK, what was the best four-ten-four
US locomotive over built?

4
00:00:10,369 --> 00:00:12,509
(Sheldon:)Trick question.
There never was one.

5
00:00:12,671 --> 00:00:15,881
(Man:)-Or was there?
-What?!

6
00:00:17,810 --> 00:00:21,020
(Man:)In 1944, the Pacific Railroad
built number 6131,

7
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:22,960
(Man:)which rearranged
the drivers and cylinders,

8
00:00:23,115 --> 00:00:24,895
(Man:)solving the problem of the Q-1,

9
00:00:25,050 --> 00:00:26,860
(Man:)creating a duplex-drive
four-four-six-four.

10
00:00:27,019 --> 00:00:30,729
(Sheldon:)In what world is a
four-four-six-four a four-ten-four?

11
00:00:30,890 --> 00:00:32,460
A world I don't want to live in!

12
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:36,560
(Howard:)Seriously, I no longer want
to live in this world.

13
00:00:38,164 --> 00:00:41,234
(Man:)Hold on to your conductor's hat.
You crank the second and third axles,

14
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:43,570
(Man:)creating a pair of
internal connecting rods,

15
00:00:43,736 --> 00:00:46,686
and boom! Four-ten-four.
If you think about it,

16
00:00:46,839 --> 00:00:49,219
(Man:)the Q-2 was like the four-ten-four
America never made.

17
00:00:49,375 --> 00:00:51,915
(Sheldon:)I may never stop thinking about it.

18
00:00:52,077 --> 00:00:54,417
(Sheldon:)Amy, what are the odds
we run into this guy?

19
00:00:54,580 --> 00:00:59,020
(Waiter:)Better than you think.

